Lint warns when an acceptance check reads like a question
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DESCRIPTION
hug task lint flags an acceptance check that is really a question to a person. Such a check is easy
to tick by mistake, and nobody is asked. The finding names the check, and its fix: line runs hug
task ask with the check's text.

PURPOSE
Jørgen 2026-11-19 08:55Z: questions today look like acceptance criteria. A question belongs
where a person is asked and answers it.

ACCEPTANCE
  ☐ 1. A check that ends in '?' is a lint finding, with a fix: line that runs hug task ask (test)
  ☐ 2. A check that starts with Should, Can or Do (English only) is a finding too (test)
  ☐ 3. hug task lint --json gives the finding the code check-is-question (test)

FILES (1)
  ⎘ history.sdd  1.1 KB  resolved marks: who asked what, and what changed





